-- title:
--   Elementary properties of the blow-up chart C[J/t]
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring and $K$ a field that is an $A$-algebra, let $C$ be an $A$-subalgebra of $K$, let $J$ be an ideal of $C$, and let $t \in A$ be an element whose image $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A\,K\,t$ in $K$ is non-zero. Let $B$ be an $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which is assumed equal to the restriction of scalars to $A$ of the $C$-subalgebra of $K$ generated by the set of those $x \in K$ for which $x \cdot \mathrm{algebraMap}\,A\,K\,t$ equals the image in $K$ of some $i \in J$ — that is, $B = C[J/t]$. The conclusion is the conjunction of six assertions: (1) $C \le B$ as subalgebras of $K$; (2) for every $b \in B$ there is $n \in \mathbb{N}$ with $t^n b \in C$ (the image of $t$ being used); (3) if every $f \in K$ admits $g, h \in C$ with $h \neq 0$ in $K$ and $f h = g$, then every $f \in K$ admits such $g, h$ in $B$; (4) if $J$ is finitely generated and $C$ is of finite type as an $A$-algebra, then so is $B$; (5) every $i \in J$ has image of the form $t \cdot b$ with $b \in B$; and (6) for every ideal $Q$ of $B$ containing the image of $t$ in $B$, and every $i \in J$ whose image lies in $B$, the corresponding element of $B$ lies in $Q$.
--
--   These are the elementary algebraic properties of an affine chart $C[J/t]$ of the blow-up of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ along $J$: the chart contains $C$, is contained in $C[1/t]$, has the same field of fractions, is of finite type when $J$ is, and in it the ideal $J$ becomes generated by $t$. It is used in the construction of blow-up charts on auxiliary models of modular curves, where the clauses supply the containment and fraction-field statements, the finite-type property of the chart algebra, and the location of its primes above $t$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Subalgebra_le_and_exists_pow_mul_mem_and_finiteType_of_eq_restrictScalars_adjoin_div.lean

